{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZvTTP9CDjb48b2XAykY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the codebase. Let me document my findings and move to the design phase.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `Order.kt:11-16` - Order data class lacks status field\n- `OrderController.kt:21-34` - POST /orders endpoint for creation\n- `OrderController.kt:36-42` - GET /orders/{orderId} endpoint\n- `OrderRepository.kt` - In-memory repository with save/findById methods\n- `Shipment.kt:23-27` - ShipmentStatus enum already exists (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- `ShipmentController.kt:26-43` - POST /shipments endpoint\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt` - Needs method to find shipments by orderId\n- `ApiExceptions.kt` - ConflictException and ResourceNotFoundException exist\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` - ErrorCode enum needs new codes for cancel scenarios\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt` - Centralized error mapping\n\n**Conventions observed:**\n- Error responses use error envelope with `$.error.code`, `$.error.message`, `$.error.fields`\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses; status codes and messages are in one place\n- Test pattern uses MockMvc with status/jsonPath assertions to verify both codes and error shapes\n- In-memory repositories using ConcurrentHashMap for test isolation\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` - add OrderStatus enum and status field (unavoidable)\n2. `OrderController.kt` - add cancel endpoint, inject ShipmentRepository (unavoidable)\n3. `ShipmentRepository.kt` - add findByOrderId method (unavoidable)\n4. `ShipmentController.kt` - validate order status on shipment create (unavoidable)\n5. `ApiError.kt` - add error codes (unavoidable)\n6. `OrderControllerTest.kt` - add cancel tests (unavoidable)\n7. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - add shipment-on-cancelled-order test (unavoidable)\n\n**Risks:**\n- State consistency: Ensure no partial updates if CONFIRMED shipment exists\n- Idempotency: Second cancel of same order must succeed with no changes\n- Integration: Shipment creation must check order status before creating\n\n**Open questions:** None - requirement is fully specified.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Add `OrderStatus` enum with `ACTIVE` and `CANCELLED` values; add `status: OrderStatus` field to `Order` data class; default newly created orders to `ACTIVE`.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt** - No changes needed; existing save/findById is sufficient for persisting status changes.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to support finding all shipments for an order during cancel validation.\n\n4. **OrderController.kt** - \n   - Inject `InMemoryShipmentRepository`\n   - Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that:\n     - Returns 404 if order not found\n     - Returns 200 with unchanged order if already CANCELLED (idempotent)\n     - Checks if any shipment with this orderId has status CONFIRMED; if yes, throw 409 ConflictException and change nothing\n     - If validation passes, set order status to CANCELLED\n     - For each CREATED shipment of that order, change its status to CANCELLED\n     - Save updated order and return it\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** - \n   - Inject `InMemoryOrderRepository`\n   - In create endpoint, before saving shipment, fetch order; if order status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with 409\n\n6. **ApiError.kt** - Add two error codes:\n   - `ORDER_NOT_FOUND` (already exists, no change)\n   - `ORDER_CANCELLED_CONFLICT` (new, for when shipment created on cancelled order)\n   - `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` (new, for when trying to cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment)\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Add tests:\n   - Cancel an ACTIVE order succeeds, order becomes CANCELLED, CREATED shipments become CANCELLED\n   - Cancel already CANCELLED order succeeds, changes nothing\n   - Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409, order stays ACTIVE\n   - Cancel non-existent order returns 404\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add test:\n   - Creating shipment for cancelled order returns 409\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- Considered making OrderStatus a String enum instead of separate data class, but separate enum is more type-safe and matches Kotlin conventions used in ShipmentStatus.\n- Considered whether OrderRepository needs update/delete methods, but simple replacement via save() suffices for in-memory storage.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\nCase 1: Cancel ACTIVE order (no CONFIRMED shipments)\n- Input: POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n- OrderController.cancel receives orderId\n- Load order from repository → check status is ACTIVE ✓\n- Query shipments for this orderId → no CONFIRMED found ✓\n- Update order.status = CANCELLED → save\n- For each CREATED shipment: status = CANCELLED → save each\n- Response: 200 OK with updated Order body\n\nCase 2: Cancel already CANCELLED order (idempotent)\n- Input: POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n- Load order → status is CANCELLED\n- Early return with 200 OK and unchanged order\n- Nothing changed\n\nCase 3: Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment (rejected)\n- Input: POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n- Load order → status is ACTIVE ✓\n- Query shipments → one has status CONFIRMED\n- Throw ConflictException(ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT)\n- Response: 409 Conflict via GlobalExceptionHandler\n- Order and shipments remain unchanged\n\nCase 4: Cancel non-existent order\n- Input: POST /orders/O-missing/cancel\n- Load order → null\n- Throw ResourceNotFoundException(ORDER_NOT_FOUND)\n- Response: 404 Not Found\n\nCase 5: Create shipment on CANCELLED order\n- Input: POST /shipments (orderId=O-1)\n- Load order → status is CANCELLED\n- Throw ConflictException(ORDER_CANCELLED_CONFLICT)\n- Response: 409 Conflict\n- Shipment not created\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\nNew tests in OrderControllerTest:\n- `cancel ACTIVE order transitions to CANCELLED` - creates order, creates CREATED shipment, cancels order, verifies order status and shipment status changed\n- `cancel already CANCELLED order idempotently succeeds` - cancels twice, second time returns 200 unchanged\n- `cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment rejects with 409` - creates order, creates shipment, confirms it (write directly to repo), attempts cancel, verify 409 and error code\n- `cancel non-existent order returns 404` - attempt cancel on missing orderId, verify 404 and error code\n\nNew tests in ShipmentControllerTest:\n- `create shipment on CANCELLED order returns 409` - cancels order then attempts shipment creation, verify 409 with correct error code\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1417,"cache_read_input_tokens":20994,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1417},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c921ba30-fc96-4eef-b2bf-f641d649d452","uuid":"5b18272b-12a3-4446-af24-54518da32ad3","timestamp":"2026-09-30T16:15:49.661Z","request_id":"req_011CfZvTSzLTSwGYBqY61u2c"}
