**\n\n- **Order.kt**: Added OrderStatus enum and status field with ACTIVE default - necessary to track order lifecycle ✓\n- **ApiError.kt**: Added two error codes (ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT, ORDER_CANCELLED_CONFLICT) - necessary for new error scenarios ✓\n- **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Added findByOrderId method - necessary to validate CONFIRMED shipments during cancel ✓\n- **OrderController.kt**: Added cancel endpoint with:\n  - 404 on unknown order ✓\n  - Early return with idempotent behavior for CANCELLED orders ✓\n  - 409 conflict if CONFIRMED shipments exist (all-or-nothing atomicity) ✓\n  - Cancels order and its CREATED shipments ✓\n  - Injects ShipmentRepository for validation - necessary for correct behavior ✓\n- **ShipmentController.kt**: Added order status check in create - necessary to prevent shipments on cancelled orders ✓\n- **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Added 5 new tests covering all new scenarios - necessary for verification ✓\n- **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Added 1 new test covering shipment-on-cancelled-order scenario - necessary for verification ✓\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All acceptance criteria are met, all error cases are covered, all edge cases (idempotency, atomicity) are handled correctly.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\n**Requirement:** Add a cancel order endpoint that allows customers to cancel active orders (with status-based validation), preventing shipment creation on cancelled orders, while making the operation idempotent.\n\n**Changed:**\n- Order.kt - Added OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and status field with default ACTIVE value\n- OrderController.kt - Added POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with proper validation and idempotency; injected ShipmentRepository\n- ShipmentRepository.kt - Added findByOrderId method to find shipments by order ID for validation\n- ShipmentController.kt - Added order status validation to prevent shipment creation on cancelled orders; injected OrderRepository\n- ApiError.kt - Added ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT and ORDER_CANCELLED_CONFLICT error codes\n- OrderControllerTest.kt - Added 5 comprehensive tests covering cancel scenarios (ACTIVE→CANCELLED, idempotency, CONFIRMED blocking, 404 handling, status in GET)\n- ShipmentControllerTest.kt - Added 1 test for shipment creation on cancelled order rejection\n\n**Tests:**\n- `cancel ACTIVE order transitions to CANCELLED and cancels CREATED shipments` - Verifies order status changes, CREATED shipments are cancelled, and both changes persist\n- `cancel already CANCELLED order idempotently succeeds` - Verifies repeated cancel succeeds without side effects\n- `cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment rejects with 409` - Verifies 409 response and atomicity (no partial updates)\n- `cancel non-existent order returns 404` - Verifies proper 404 error with correct error code\n- `newly created order has ACTIVE status` - Verifies default status assignment\n- `create shipment for cancelled order returns 409` - Verifies shipment creation rejection with correct error code\n\n**Verification:** Ran `./mvnw test` from sample-service/ directory. Result: BUILD SUCCESS with 19 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, 0 skipped. All existing tests continue to pass; all new tests pass.\n\n**Not done:** Nothing. All acceptance criteria satisfied, all tests passing, all changes necessary and no extraneous modifications."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3353,"cache_read_input_tokens":35675,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3353},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c921ba30-fc96-4eef-b2bf-f641d649d452","uuid":"b9513c1c-84f3-4ed4-a78b-fb1a42d9a295","timestamp":"2026-09-30T16:17:31.045Z","request_id":"req_011CfZvbVJTVvYygCNvVz6Uy"}
